>Q.  What do I do to keep my equip safe from Nymphs???

1) Appeal to the nymphs vanity.  They always like to look their best.
   They can be bribed with the occasional ring.  Or you can give them
   a good luck at just how beautiful they are.

2) Don't carry much useful stuff when you visit the nymph.  The more
   stuff you carry that you don't care about, the more likely she'll
   steal something you don't care about.  How you want to interpret
   this idea, I'll leave to you.

3) Leave them alone.  They usually don't move very quickly, and
   are usually asleep when first encountered.  As long as you don't
   wake them up, your stuff is safe.

4) Let your pet deal with the situation.  After all, your pet usually
   doesn't carry anything worth stealing.  I still do occasionally
   find it odd that Fido never feels jumpy right after a meal.

